---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { formatDate, formatTags, getVisiblePosts } from '../lib/posts';

const posts = await getVisiblePosts();
---
<Base
  title="Bruno Bahri · application security"
  description="Field notes on application security for multi-tenant SaaS: sandboxing untrusted code, authorization, authentication, SSRF and audit trails."
>
<section class="hero">
<p class="prompt">$ whoami</p>
<h1>Bruno Bahri. Application security for multi-tenant SaaS.</h1>
<p class="lede">Field notes from the defender's side: sandboxing untrusted code, authorization flaws, session security, SSRF and audit trails. Bugs are written up only after they are fixed.</p>
</section>
<section class="block">
<p class="prompt">$ cat focus.txt</p>
<ul class="focus">
<li>untrusted code execution and sandboxing</li>
<li>authorization and tenant isolation</li>
<li>authentication, sessions and 2FA</li>
<li>SSRF and egress control</li>
<li>audit logging and detection</li>
<li>secure code review</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="posts" class="block">
<p class="prompt">$ ls -lt posts/</p>
{posts.length === 0 ? (
<p class="muted">total 0</p>
) : (
<ul class="posts">
{posts.map((post) => (
<li>
<a href={`/posts/${post.id}`}>
<span class="date">{formatDate(post.data.date)}</span>
<span class="entry">
<span class="title">{post.data.title}</span>
<span class="tags">{formatTags(post.data.tags)}</span>
</span>
</a>
</li>
))}
</ul>
)}
</section>
<section id="about" class="block">
<p class="prompt">$ cat about.txt</p>
<p class="about">Backend engineer leading security for a Brazilian B2B SaaS. Day to day that means reviewing code for access-control and isolation flaws, sandboxing customer code, hardening authentication and keeping an audit trail. The employer stays anonymous, and nothing here describes a weakness that is still open.</p>
<ul class="links">
<li><a href="https://github.com/brunobahri">github.com/brunobahri</a></li>
<li><a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security contact</a></li>
<li><a href="/rss.xml">rss</a></li>
</ul>
</section>
</Base>
